                <pb facs="0850" n="756" sameAs="frus:frus1930v03/pg756"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">823.01/22: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Peru</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Dearing</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lima</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-09-16T12:00:00-05:00">September 16,
                        1930—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 6:15 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>215. My 207, September 13, 10 a.m. [<hi rendition="#italic">p.m.</hi>] British
                    Chargé d’Affaires has just informed me Great Britain will, on September 18th,
                    recognize junta in Peru and in the Argentine Republic<anchor n="11"
                        xml:id="d696-f1"/> simultaneously as the governments of their respective
                    countries and that this action is due to your statement to British Ambassador in
                    Washington that you were favorable to recognition, would shortly direct that
                    recognition be accorded to Peru and Argentina at the same time but wished to
                    discuss the situation with the President before issuing instructions.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dearing</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
